; THE PRICED ECONOMY. The same allotment of steel, the same three plants, the
; same centre-and-allocator machinery — and one different guard.
;
; Everything about the world lives in ../libraries/economy.lib.writ and is
; IDENTICAL to `planned.writ` next door: the same plants with the same needs, the
; same allocation rule reading the same `ask`, the same one-way commitment. The
; transitions have the same NAMES, so the same claims file can be put to both.
;
; Here, the signal is a BID, and a bid is backed. Asking for the steel means
; offering to pay for it out of the plant's own budget, so a plant that does not
; need the steel is not merely unwise to ask — the move is not available to it:
; `(when (and (not (is P.ask LEVEL)) (is P.need LEVEL)))`.
;
; That guard is the entire claim being made about prices, and it is worth being
; blunt about what it does and does not assert. It does NOT say markets are
; efficient, fair, or good. It says one thing: a signal that costs the sender
; something is a signal whose value cannot be raised for free, so it stays tied
; to the sender's own situation — which is the one thing that makes `P.need`
; reachable by an allocator standing outside the plant. There is no other
; channel in either file, and there is no other difference between them.

(load "../libraries/economy.lib.writ")

(use economy)
(initial year-one)

; THE SIGNAL: a bid. Same shape, same name, one extra conjunct — the bid must be
; backed by the plant's own situation. This is the one datum that differs from
; planned.writ.
(form (request NAME P LEVEL)
  (transition NAME
    (when (and (not (is P.ask LEVEL))
               (is P.need LEVEL)))
    (do (set P.ask LEVEL))))

(request ask-clinic-high   clinic        high)
(request ask-clinic-low    clinic        low)
(request ask-tractor-high  tractor-works high)
(request ask-tractor-low   tractor-works low)
(request ask-monument-high monument      high)
(request ask-monument-low  monument      low)

; THE ALLOCATION and the COMMITMENT, from the library — byte-identical to
; planned.writ. `allocate-monument` is written down here exactly as it is there:
; the rules permit the monument to be given the steel. It never is, and no guard
; in this file forbids it — the move simply never becomes available, because the
; signal it waits on cannot be produced.
(allocate allocate-clinic   clinic)
(allocate allocate-tractor  tractor-works)
(allocate allocate-monument monument)

(build build-clinic   clinic)
(build build-tractor  tractor-works)
(build build-monument monument)
